ory\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Gilmer County came in under 90% of normal in September to October in 34 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair of months. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 52% of normal in August to September and 72% in September to October. So far in 2026 it got 51% of normal in January to February on the middle of the grids. Grid 22698 had its driest year in 1988 at 69% of normal.</p>"}
